course: dictionary
lesson: 15871
title: Unhinged: wild, slang or literal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Unhinged» can describe someone who seems wild, crazy or out of control, as in «The villain was completely unhinged, shrieking at the storm.» The clues are shrieking and the storm. Wild, loud behaviour tells you the word means out of control.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «The garden gate hung unhinged after the storm.» Here it means the gate was taken off its hinges. Look at the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Online and among friends, people say «That video is unhinged!» to mean it is very weird or over the top, often as a joke. This is slang, so it is informal and fine for chatty talk, but not for school essays.
explain: Be kind with this word. Calling a real person «unhinged» because of how they look or act can hurt, especially if they have a mental illness. Save it for stories, funny videos and things, not for putting down real people.
fact: «Unhinged» means mentally unbalanced, or wild, crazy and frightening in how someone acts.
fact: «Unhinged» can also mean a door or gate taken off its hinges.
fact: In slang, «unhinged» is used jokingly for something very weird or over the top.
fact: «Unhinged» is informal, so keep it for stories and casual talk, not formal writing.
fact: Calling real people unhinged can be hurtful, especially to people with mental illness.
exercise: «The villain in the story was unhinged, shrieking at the storm.» What does unhinged mean here? | Tied up with rope | Hungry | Calm and quiet | *Wild and out of control
exercise: «The garden gate hung unhinged after the storm.» What does unhinged mean in this sentence? | Painted bright red | *Taken off its hinges | Very loud | Locked tight
exercise: Online, a friend says «That video is unhinged!» What do they most likely mean? | The video is very sad and quiet | *It is very weird and over the top, said as a joke | The video is about door hinges | The video is an old film
test: Which is the best reason not to call a real person unhinged? | It means they are very tall | *It can hurt people, especially those with mental illness | It is only used for doors | It is a formal word for happy
test: The story's villain was ___ and shouted at everyone in the street. | *Unhinged | Calm | Tired | Hungry
exam: Which meaning fits best in «He drove unhinged through the town, honking and yelling»? | Asleep | Very tidy | *Wild and out of control | Slowly and safely
